1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
[narrator] Leol has pursued Morel
into an underground church,

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
where they will now face off in battle.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,000
[chuckles]

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,000
[screams]

5
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,000
[singer singing in English]

6
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

7
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,000
[singer singing in English]

8
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

9
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,000
My Tube ability summons the ocean!

10
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
[Morel grunts]

11
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,000
[gasps]

12
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,000
[Leol] Well? What do you think
of my big wave? Huh?

13
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Just stay still,
and you'll die even quicker.

14
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
[Leol] He's making a boat out of smoke?

15
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
I see. You can ride on top of it.

16
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,000
[both grunt]

17
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
[Leol] Ha!

18
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Do you really think
that's enough to tame my waves?

19
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Huh. This one is one of my original moves.

20
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
[yelling]

21
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Vortex!

22
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,000
[inhaling]

23
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,000
[Morel] Damn it. The current's so strong
I can't tell up from down.

24
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
This is bad.

25
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Here goes.

26
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Then finish him with a harpoon from above.

27
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
by traveling at the speed of sound.

28
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Take this!

29
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
[gasps]

30
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Wait. He disappeared?

31
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Impossible.

32
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
The whirlpool
should have kept him trapped.

33
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
He had no way to escape.

34
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Ah.

35
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Bastard.

36
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Okay, then. Looks like it's my turn now.

37
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:48,000
is that your ability
somehow uses the abilities of others.

38
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Or you could be getting all your orders
from somebody else.

39
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
[growls]

40
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,000
[Morel] If he's increasing his risk
by limiting his hearing

41
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:11,000
in order to upgrade his ability,
he shouldn't be able to hear me.

42
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
What's the third thing?

43
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Third is your life span.

44
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Tube once belonged to a Hunter I knew
named Grachan, not you.

45
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:28,000
He was helping to exterminate Chimera Ants
so I suppose you must have defeated him.

46
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
And since you stole his ability,
you deserve to die.

47
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
[chuckles] I'm only borrowing it.

48
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Only borrowing it, huh? [scoffs]

49
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
That's a lowlife thief's excuse,
if I ever heard one.

50
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Huh?

51
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:07,000
[Leol] I can see that arguing with you
is just a waste of my time.

52
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:13,000
I'd like to get my hands on his ability,
but defeating him's more important.

53
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
No.

54
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
He was confident in his lung capacity,

55
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:27,000
so he can survive for 10,
maybe 20 minutes.

56
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:33,000
No, wait. It's possible
he could stay underwater for even longer,

57
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
-[bubbles popping]
-Huh?

58
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
There you are.

59
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Now hold still,
and I'll stab you with my harpoon.

60
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
-[bubbles popping]
-Huh?

61
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
I get it.

62
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:14,000
It's possible he could've formed his smoke
into a hose with multiple branches.

63
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:18,000
That way,
he wouldn't have to reveal his position.

64
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
No, it's not.

65
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
The bubbles are camouflage.

66
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Did he escape?

67
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:50,000
I told Welfin and Bloster to stay back
so I could take all the credit.

68
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
[gasping, groaning]

69
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
My head's spinning, and my chest hurts.

70
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
[gasping]

71
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
My board's gone!

72
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,000
I'm too unstable to keep it activated.

73
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[straining] Can't move or breathe.

74
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:23,000
My ability stopped working,
but the water's still here?

75
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Not good.

76
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
I let him think he had the advantage
so I could turn the tables on him.

77
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:40,000
But it looks like the one
who was backed into a corner was me.

78
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Is this it?

79
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Is this the end?

80
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:09,000
So he was using a hose made of smoke
to send air bubbles everywhere.

81
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
It's CO2.

82
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,000
[narrator] Morel used
his immense lung capacity

83
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
to suck in the stagnant air
trapped in the church

84
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
[Morel] You might not have realized it,

85
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
but my attacks began even before yours.

86
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
If what he said was true,

87
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Grachan should be getting his ability back
right about now.

88
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,000
[Bizeff snoring]

89
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
[Palm] I'll be free to move around
for a few hours.

90
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:27,000
In that time,
I have to see them with my own eyes.

91
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
I've watched Bizeff's movements
with my crystal ball.

92
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
[clanging]

93
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
[gasping]

94
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:05,000
They're close. Right above me.

95
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,000
[gulps]

96
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
[breath shaking]

97
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,000
[gasps]

98
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,000
[whimpering]

99
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
[people speaking indistinctly]

100
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
[groaning]

101
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,000
[gasps]

102
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Oh. You're up. That's good.

103
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
You were out for two whole days.

104
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Two days? I need to get going.

105
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Whoa! Just take it easy.
Your wounds still need to heal.

106
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:18,000
[grunts] But there are things
that I have to do.

107
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Idiot! You were on the verge of death.

108
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
You can't just go running off now.

109
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,000
You'll need to rest before--

110
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
-[doctor] Ah, look who's awake.
-[Ikalgo] Huh?

111
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
How wonderful.

112
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:32,000
[Killua] Thanks for helping,
but I'll be checking out now.

113
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Not until you pay your bill.

114
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:39,000
And the total comes to 1.8 million Jenny.

115
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:43,000
If you can't pay,
then I'll accept body parts instead.

116
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:47,000
I don't have my wallet with me,
so I'll wire it as soon as I get back.

117
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Do you really think that I'm stupid enough
to take an IOU from you?

118
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,000
[line ringing]

119
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,000
It's 10,000 Jenny for each minute.

120
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Quiet! Just shut up, and go away!

121
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,000
[Gon] Hello?

122
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
[Killua] I'll tell you when I see you.

123
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
An enemy gave me a little bit of trouble.

124
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,000
I've been in the hospital.

125
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
That sucks.

126
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,000
But thanks for calling.

127
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
So you're okay, right?

128
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Yeah. Heading back soon.

129
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,000
[Killua] Oh.

130
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,000
[Gon] Let's talk it over
as soon as possible, okay?

131
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:49,000
[Killua] Sounds good, but, hey,
I need you to send money to an account.

132
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Do that and we can rendezvous later today.

133
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,000
[chuckles]

134
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[Gon] I guess that just leaves Palm.

135
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
You mean you haven't
been able to reach her yet?

136
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,000
What about Pitou's En?

137
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,000
With that, she'd be found,
maybe already has.

138
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,000
I imagine that she's down
in the underground hangar.

139
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
she won't be able to get out.

140
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
[Gon] How's Mr. Knov doing?

141
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
He's, uh…

142
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
probably done fighting.

143
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:40,000
But he did manage to plant the exits,

144
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
so it hasn't changed our plan.

145
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,000
[stammers]

146
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Right. I'm good to go.

147
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,000
[stammers]

148
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
-[door opens]
-[doctor] Okay.

149
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Your payment finally came through.

150
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,000
You're all cleared to leave now,
so get out.

151
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,000
[door opens]

152
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,000
-[Killua] What are you doing?
-Uh…

153
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
-Let's go.
-[stammers]

154
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,000
We're gonna go join my friends.

155
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,000
I'll introduce you.

156
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Uh…

157
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,000
But…

158
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,000
[gasps] Uh, wait.

159
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,000
I mean…

160
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,000
Is it really okay?

161
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
I mean, I'm just a…

162
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,000
You're sure?

163
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,000
I can go, too?

164
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:19,000
[Killua] I'm sure!

165
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Well? Are you coming or not?

166
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:24,000
[Ikalgo] Yeah, I'll go! I'll go with you!

167
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
Let's just get one thing straight.

168
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,000
and I end up helping you out,

169
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,000
[Killua] I'm sure that you and I

170
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
will be helping each other out
all the time from now on,

171
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,000
It's not worth it.

172
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:38,000
Killua, I… I'm so happy, I could die!

173
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Wait! What the hell
are you crying about, huh?

174
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,000
'Cause you're doing this
for someone like me.

175
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
-[sobbing]
-[sighs] Give me a break.

176
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:58,000
it's more brutal than what you're used to.

177
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
[gasps]

178
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
It may seem similar,

179
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:06,000
but there's a huge difference between
risking your life and throwing it away.

180
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:19,000
But if you can take
perfect care of your body

181
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:22,000
and drink poison
that's barely under the lethal dose

182
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:25,000
without the least hesitation,
you can survive.

183
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:47,000
Thanks for the warning,
but all I see is paradise.

184
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
I'll go, no matter the cost.

185
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,000
I've seen the other side.

186
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,000
I have a connection to it now.

187
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:03,000
-I know it really exists.
-[closing theme song playing]

188
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:08,000
And now I know that even someone like me
can go there!

189
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:11,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

190
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
[Killua] Four-three-three-two?

191
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:41,000
[Gon] Hey, that's my phone number!

192
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:44,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
